<title>UK: UK card spending up yr/yr 17.3 pct in March -CCRG.</title>
<headline>UK card spending up yr/yr 17.3 pct in March -CCRG.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Credit Card Research Group, representing major UK credit and debit card issuers, released the following consumer spending figures for March 1997 -</p>
<p> CARD EXPENDITURE (in million stg) *   March 97 March 96  % change</p>
<p> All sectors - total		   7,441     6,342    17.3</p>
<p> Food and drink			  1,895     1,678    12.9</p>
<p> Mixed business			    544	 480    13.5</p>
<p> Clothing				    407	 351    15.8</p>
<p> Household				   711	 521    36.5</p>
<p> Motoring				    1,046     888    17.8</p>
<p> Entertainment			     408	 353    15.4</p>
<p> Hotels					252	 216    17.1</p>
<p> Travel					742	 673    10.3</p>
<p> Services				    645	 481    34.2</p>
<p>Credit Card Research Group director Elizabeth Philips said, gardeners, do-it-yourself enthusiasts and home decorators helped boost overall card spending in March. &quot;The combination of unusually fine weather and strong interest in the property market meant that the household sector saw the highest annual increase since card spending was recorded of 37 percent.&quot;</p>
<p>NOTE * figures adjusted for variations in the number of processing days between months.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
